@startuml Timing Diagram
!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam defaultFontSize 12

title Diagrama de Temporización - Señales de Control

binary
  title STEP Pulse (RC1/NCO1OUT)
  0 as step_low
  1 as step_high

  0.000 as step_0
  step_low -down- step_high
  step_high -up- step_low
  step_low -down- step_high
  step_high -up- step_low
  step_low -down- step_high
  step_high -up- step_low
  step_low -down- step_high
  step_high -up- step_low
  0.008 as step_end

binary
  title DIR Signal (RC2)
  0 as dir_0
  
  0.002 as dir_change
  dir_0 -up-> 1 : Direction change
  1 as dir_1
  dir_1 -down-> 0
  0 as dir_0b
  0.008 as dir_end

concise
  title Telemetry Timer (Timer 2 - 100ms interrupt)
  
  0.000 as t0
  : 0
  0.025 as t1
  : 0
  0.050 as t2
  : 0
  0.075 as t3
  : 0
  0.100 as t4
  : 1
  : ISR triggers
  0.200 as t5
  : 0
  0.300 as t6
  : 1
  : ISR triggers

note top of step_0
  STEP frequency depends on:
  - Configured velocity (mm/min)
  - STEPS_PER_MM (320)
  - Microstepping mode
  
  Current: Fixed frequency
  Future: Variable (ramp profile)
end note

note right of dir_change
  Direction changes only
  when motor stops or
  during G92 command
end note

note bottom of t4
  Every 100ms:
  - Read position counter
  - Send via UART (if enabled)
  - Format: "X:xx.xx"
  
  Controlled by M120/M121
end note

footer
  Time scale: milliseconds (ms)
  STEP pulse train example shown
endfooter

@enduml
